    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `build_client` in `app/llm_client.py` and it meets all four requirements. `pytest -q` passes (1 test).\n\n**One thing you might not expect:** openai 3.19.2 uses **`httpx2`**, not `httpx`. So the client is built with `openai.DefaultHttpx2Client`, which also keeps the SDK's default connection limits and redirect handling. The stub transport in your tests needs to be an `httpx2` transport (for example `httpx2.MockTransport`). No dependencies were added, since `httpx2` is already installed as part of openai.\n\nHow each requirement is handled:\n1. **Timeouts:** connect is 5s; read, write and pool are 30s. I set this on the HTTP client and also on `OpenAI(timeout=...)`. The second one matters because the SDK sends its own timeout with every request, which would otherwise override the HTTP client's.\n2. **Retries:** `max_retries=2`.\n3. **Logging:** a request event hook logs `\"<METHOD> <URL>\"` at INFO on the `app.http` logger. It runs for every attempt, including retries.\n4. **Transport:** if `transport` is given, it's passed to the HTTP client.\n\n**Check:** I ran a separate script with a stub transport that always returns HTTP 500. It showed 3 attempts (1 plus 2 retries), each logged as `app.http INFO GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models`. Every request carried `{'connect': 5.0, 'read': 30.0, 'write': 30.0, 'pool': 30.0}`.\n\n**Cleanup needed:** that script is still in the project root as `_chk.py`, because the command to delete it needed approval. Please delete it, or approve the removal and I'll do it."
  },
